{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Minor_improvement)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Minor improvement)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Initially, a spinner points west. Chenille moves it clockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c1f128b6984cebccb828f839748e2c894485dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\dfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> revolutions and then counterclockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd187a7fe0e2167ff693aab9c1a76cc2d7d4f44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\dfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> revolutions. In what direction does the spinner point after the two moves?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39f6c3905c23037677847312e6fe6254d0dd9923.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(96); draw(circle((0,0),1),linewidth(1)); draw((0,0.75)--(0,1.25),linewidth(1)); draw((0,-0.75)--(0,-1.25),linewidth(1)); draw((0.75,0)--(1.25,0),linewidth(1)); draw((-0.75,0)--(-1.25,0),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$N$&quot;,(0,1.25), N); label(&quot;$W$&quot;,(-1.25,0), W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(1.25,0), E); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,(0,-1.25), S); draw((0,0)--(-0.5,0),EndArrow);[/asy]\" width=\"162\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc93ced8936cb62f505ed4344bb1e2df016c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{north} \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{east} \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{south} \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{west} \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{northwest}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the spinner goes clockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c1f128b6984cebccb828f839748e2c894485dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\dfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> revolutions and then counterclockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd187a7fe0e2167ff693aab9c1a76cc2d7d4f44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\dfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> revolutions, it ultimately goes counterclockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/d/2bdb7edebcb4377bdfea8c666e1fac6b8dbf0ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> which brings the spinner pointing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e55bb4c5a7825d78a46f347b7b5fe5af4422822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{east}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Minor_improvement.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Minor_improvement)\">Solution 2 (Minor improvement)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Minor improvement)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that full revolutions do not matter, so this is equivalent to going clockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415dd5722f2b57ce55e47766ccb11a0cdc4eb051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> revolutions and then counterclockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa608ff4fd7754c4ff82a2e8ac12c2fbf6ab80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> revolutions, making it ultimately go counterclockwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4a7df1100efe353cc612d5d1c289c22d5bf8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, having the spinner point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e55bb4c5a7825d78a46f347b7b5fe5af4422822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{east}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~JeffersonJ\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vhRtbl9iV30\">https://youtu.be/vhRtbl9iV30</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 8\">2006 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=